<div class="legal">
	<section data-legal-id="scope">
		<h2>Photographs licence</h2>
		<div>
			The photographs in the galleries of <strong>{{ legal_var('site-name') }}</strong> are works protected by copyright. Each one states, under it, its author and the licence it is published under.
		</div>
		<div>
			A gallery may be published under a Creative Commons licence; where no licence is stated, all rights are reserved.
		</div>
	</section>

	<section data-legal-id="all-rights-reserved">
		<h2>All rights reserved</h2>
		<div>
			Without permission, only a copy strictly kept for private use and a short quotation naming the author and the source are allowed, under the terms of article L. 122-5 of the French Intellectual Property Code.
		</div>
		<div>
			Any other use requires the author's prior written consent: publication on a website or a social network, press, publishing, printing, commercial or advertising use, alteration. Within the meaning of article L. 122-5-3 of the same code, the author objects to text and data mining of their photographs, including for training artificial intelligence systems.
		</div>
	</section>

	<section data-legal-id="creative-commons">
		<h2>Creative Commons licences</h2>
		<div>
			A photograph published under a Creative Commons licence may be used under the terms of that licence, whose text is reached through the link under the photograph. It must be credited by naming its author, the licence and a link to the photograph.
		</div>
		<div>
			Any use that licence does not allow, for instance a commercial use under an "NC" licence, still requires the author's written consent.
		</div>
	</section>

	<section data-legal-id="request">
		<h2>Requesting a licence</h2>
		<div>
			A request for use is sent to <strong>{{ legal_var('site-contact-email') }}</strong>, stating the address of the photograph or photographs concerned, the intended use, the medium, the duration and the territory of distribution.
		</div>
		<div>
			The licence, free or paid depending on the use, is only acquired once the author has agreed in writing, setting its terms.
		</div>
	</section>

	<section data-legal-id="prints">
		<h2>Prints</h2>
		<div>
			Buying a print, where one is offered, transfers ownership of the object and not the copyright in the photograph, in accordance with article L. 111-3 of the French Intellectual Property Code: it allows neither reproducing nor distributing it.
		</div>
	</section>
</div>
